Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:34:07 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 08/47] Plutonium: tab automation over DevTools, SurfaceEmbed
 fixes

- Window broker: sendTabDevToolsCommand (shell document only) sends a
  DevTools protocol command to a registry tab through an untrusted
  DevToolsAgentHostClient: page domains only (Runtime, Input, Page, DOM,
  Accessibility, Emulation, Log, Network), no local files, no browser
  target. Lets the shell automate its tabs (T3 Code's preview automation).
- SurfaceEmbed plugin: the embedded page lays out at the element's own
  (untransformed) size, like an OOPIF, and rasters at the drawn scale.
  A scaled <embed> used to get a scaled-down page, drawn scaled twice.
- Performance manager: don't set a viewport intersection on an outermost
  main frame (a SurfaceEmbed tab's); it is a bad message and crashed the
  browser when the embedder's renderer went away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
